# A p-adic place for eigenform coefficients and a seed character

Theorem statement: `HorizontalPadicL.seededEigenform_padicPlace_exists_v2`
(`c03f96ff-d7e5-4a58-a233-f213d2a67e09`), by davidloeffler, 2026-09-25.

Proof: submission `f84d543b-d3e9-4a19-b199-8f69aec1bade`, by davidloeffler, 2026-09-25 (ACCEPTED);
locally adapted.

Let $f$ be a new normalized eigenform of positive level and weight at least two, let $p$ be prime,
and let $\eta$ be an algebraic Dirichlet character. There is an embedding of the common algebraic
coefficient field into $\mathbf C_p$ under which every Fourier coefficient $a_n(f)$ and every value
of $\eta$ is $p$-adically integral.

This supplies the coefficient place at which the residual representation and orderly-prime
congruences are evaluated.

## Explanation of the source proof

The Fourier coefficients of a normalized eigenform and the values of a Dirichlet character are
algebraic integers. Adjoin the finitely generated coefficient data to obtain a number field, choose
a prime above $p$, and embed its completion into $\mathbf C_p$. Algebraic integers map into the
valuation ring under this embedding, so every Fourier coefficient and every seed-character value is
$p$-adically integral. This gives the bundled p-adic place data.

